-- title:
--   Unique place above a rational valuation ring, and its rationality
-- statement:
--   Let $k_0$, $L$, $F$ be fields with $L$ of characteristic zero, equipped with $k_0$-algebra structures on $L$ and $F$ and an $L$-algebra structure on $F$ compatible with $k_0$ (a scalar tower). Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $F/k_0$ and $K_1$ an intermediate field of $L/k_0$, and assume: the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $L$, joined with $F_0$, is all of $F$; and every element of $L$ is algebraic over $K_1$. Write $F_1$ for the intermediate field $k_0$-generated by the image of $K_1$ in $F$ joined with $F_0$. Let $V_1$ be a valuation subring of $F_1$ such that every $x \in K_1$ whose image in $F$ lies in $F_1$ lies in $V_1$, assume $V_1$ is a discrete valuation ring, and assume every $v \in V_1$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $V_1$ to the image of some element of $K_1$. Then (i) there is exactly one place $P$ of $F$ over $L$ — a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\mathrm{im}(L)$, distinct from $F$, and a principal ideal ring — whose valuation subring meets $F_1$ exactly in $V_1$, i.e. $f \in \mathcal{O}_P \iff f \in V_1$ for all $f \in F_1$; and (ii) every place $P$ of $F/L$ with that property is rational, i.e. $L \to \mathcal{O}_P/\mathfrak{m}_P$ is surjective.
--
--   This is the statement that a constant field extension is unramified above a rational place: a $K_1$-rational discrete valuation ring of the level field $F_1 = k_0(K_1)\cdot F_0$ lies under a unique place of $F$ over $L$, and that place has residue field generated by the constants $L$. It is used in the construction of regular prolongations, where sections are evaluated at places of a disc.
